{
  "$defs": {
    "ADX": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Average Directional Index (Wilder) — how strongly a market trends, read by component.\n\nReferenced as `adx.adx` for the strength line and `adx.plus_di` / `adx.minus_di` for the two\ndirection lines. ⚠️ **The `adx` component has no direction**: it rises in a hard sell-off\nexactly as it does in a rally, so a rule meaning \"trending up\" needs the `DI` pair as well.\nReads the whole candle, so there is no price source to name — same argument as `PeriodParams`.",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "maxLength": 40,
          "pattern": "^[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*$",
          "title": "Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "params": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PeriodParams"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "ADX",
          "title": "Type",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "type",
        "params"
      ],
      "title": "ADX",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ATR": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Average True Range (Wilder) — the size of a typical bar, in price.\n\nTrue Range counts the gap: a bar that opens away from the previous close travelled further\nthan its own high minus its low. Used to size stops and to ask whether a market is moving\nat all.",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "maxLength": 40,
          "pattern": "^[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*$",
          "title": "Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "params": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PeriodParams"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "ATR",
          "title": "Type",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "type",
        "params"
      ],
      "title": "ATR",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "AllOf": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Logical AND.",
      "properties": {
        "all": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/Condition"
          },
          "minItems": 1,
          "title": "All",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "all"
      ],
      "title": "AllOf",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "AnyOf": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Logical OR.",
      "properties": {
        "any": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/Condition"
          },
          "minItems": 1,
          "title": "Any",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "any"
      ],
      "title": "AnyOf",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "AverageKind": {
      "enum": [
        "EMA",
        "SMA"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
    "Between": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Three operands: is `value` inside the band `[low, high]`?\n\n⚠️ **Both bounds are inclusive**, and it is written down here because \"between\" is the kind\nof word every reader is sure they already know. Exclusive would make `between 0 and 100`\nreject the two values a bounded oscillator can actually reach.\n\nA node of its own rather than an `op` on `Comparison`, because it takes three operands and\n`Comparison` takes two. Folding it in would make `right` mean one thing for seven operators\nand another for this one — and the untagged union below discriminates on *shape*, so the\ndistinct shape is what keeps a document unambiguous.\n\nThe bounds are operands, not numbers, so a band can be drawn between two indicators — a\nprice inside its own channel is `between(price.close, lower, upper)`.",
      "properties": {
        "high": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Operand"
        },
        "low": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Operand"
        },
        "op": {
          "const": "between",
          "title": "Op",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "value": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Operand"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "op",
        "value",
        "low",
        "high"
      ],
      "title": "Between",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Bollinger": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Bollinger Bands — an average with a volatility envelope, read by component.\n\n⚠️ **One indicator with three readings, not three indicators.** Declared once as `bb`, its\nbands are referenced as `bb.upper`, `bb.middle` and `bb.lower`. Three separate declarations\nwould let a document give the upper band a period of 20 and the lower one 50, and nothing\ncould object: for this schema they would be two well-formed indicators. What came out would\nbe a band whose rails describe different markets, and it would look exactly like a band.",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "maxLength": 40,
          "pattern": "^[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*$",
          "title": "Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "params": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/BollingerParams"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "BOLLINGER",
          "title": "Type",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "type",
        "params"
      ],
      "title": "Bollinger",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "BollingerParams": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A window, the price it reads, and how many deviations wide the envelope is.\n\n`deviations` is a float rather than an int because 1.5 and 2.5 are ordinary settings, and it\nis bounded above 0 exclusively: a multiplier of zero collapses the three bands onto the\naverage, which is an SMA spelled in a way that hides that it is one. The upper bound is\ngenerous — a band ten deviations out is useless, not malformed.",
      "properties": {
        "deviations": {
          "default": 2.0,
          "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
          "maximum": 10,
          "title": "Deviations",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "period": {
          "maximum": 1000,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Period",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "source": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PriceSource",
          "default": "close"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "period"
      ],
      "title": "BollingerParams",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "CandleExtremeParams": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "lookback": {
          "maximum": 100,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Lookback",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "side": {
          "enum": [
            "low",
            "high"
          ],
          "title": "Side",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "lookback",
        "side"
      ],
      "title": "CandleExtremeParams",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "CandleExtremeStop": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Stop at the low (or high) of the last N closed candles.",
      "properties": {
        "params": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/CandleExtremeParams"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "candle_extreme",
          "title": "Type",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "params"
      ],
      "title": "CandleExtremeStop",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Comparison": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A leaf: two operands and an operator.\n\n`gt` asks about this candle. `crosses_above` asks about this candle *and the\nprevious one* — it is true only on the bar where the relation flips, which is\nwhat stops a strategy from re-entering on every bar of a trend it already owns.",
      "properties": {
        "left": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Operand"
        },
        "op": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ComparisonOp"
        },
        "right": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Operand"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "op",
        "left",
        "right"
      ],
      "title": "Comparison",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ComparisonOp": {
      "enum": [
        "gt",
        "lt",
        "gte",
        "lte",
        "crosses_above",
        "crosses_below",
        "breaks_above",
        "breaks_below"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
    "Condition": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Comparison"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Between"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Trend"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/AllOf"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/AnyOf"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/NotOf"
        }
      ]
    },
    "Constant": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A literal number — the fixed side of a threshold like `RSI < 30`. It references nothing,\nso the semantic layer skips it; `inf`/`nan` are rejected because no comparison means them.",
      "properties": {
        "value": {
          "examples": [
            30,
            70,
            0.0
          ],
          "title": "Value",
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "value"
      ],
      "title": "Constant",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ContinuationParams": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "`max_bos` caps how many breaks after a change of character may still be traded.\n\n`null` is uncapped, which is the default and not a degenerate setting: \"every favourable\nbreak re-arms\" is a real reading of the method, and capping it is the experiment.",
      "properties": {
        "allow_secondary": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Allow Secondary",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "breakeven_at_r": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
              "maximum": 100,
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": 2.0,
          "title": "Breakeven At R"
        },
        "max_bos": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "maximum": 100,
              "minimum": 1,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Max Bos"
        },
        "stop_buffer": {
          "default": 0.1,
          "maximum": 10,
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Stop Buffer",
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "title": "ContinuationParams",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "EMA": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "maxLength": 40,
          "pattern": "^[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*$",
          "title": "Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "params": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PeriodSourceParams"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "EMA",
          "title": "Type",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "type",
        "params"
      ],
      "title": "EMA",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Entry": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Entry conditions per side. A strategy must trade at least one of them.",
      "properties": {
        "long": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Condition"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "short": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Condition"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        }
      },
      "title": "Entry",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Exit": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "conditions": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/Condition"
          },
          "title": "Conditions",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "stop_loss": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/CandleExtremeStop"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "take_profit": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/RiskMultipleTakeProfit"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        }
      },
      "title": "Exit",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Highest": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "The highest **high** of the N bars that closed *before* this one — a breakout's rail.\n\n⚠️ **The current bar is not in the window**, and that is what makes the level breakable:\ninclude it and `HIGHEST(20) >= high` holds on every bar of every market, so a comparison\nagainst it is constantly false and a band drawn with it is constantly true. A charting\nplatform's `ta.highest` does include the current bar and is read shifted (`[1]`); the DSL\nhas no shift for an indicator ref, so the level is defined where it can be used.\n\nHighs, not closes, so the level is where price actually traded. A breakout of it therefore\nfires on the wick, which is the classical reading and the more sensitive one; comparing\nagainst `price.close` instead is how the same channel is made to require a close beyond it.",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "maxLength": 40,
          "pattern": "^[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*$",
          "title": "Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "params": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PeriodParams"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "HIGHEST",
          "title": "Type",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "type",
        "params"
      ],
      "title": "Highest",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Indicator": {
      "discriminator": {
        "mapping": {
          "ADX": "#/$defs/ADX",
          "ATR": "#/$defs/ATR",
          "BOLLINGER": "#/$defs/Bollinger",
          "EMA": "#/$defs/EMA",
          "HIGHEST": "#/$defs/Highest",
          "LOWEST": "#/$defs/Lowest",
          "RSI": "#/$defs/RSI",
          "SMA": "#/$defs/SMA"
        },
        "propertyName": "type"
      },
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/SMA"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EMA"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/RSI"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ATR"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Highest"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Lowest"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Bollinger"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ADX"
        }
      ]
    },
    "Lowest": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "The lowest **low** of the N bars that closed before this one — the lower rail.",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "maxLength": 40,
          "pattern": "^[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*$",
          "title": "Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "params": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PeriodParams"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "LOWEST",
          "title": "Type",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "type",
        "params"
      ],
      "title": "Lowest",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Mme9BreakoutParams": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "The break of the candle that closed across the MME9 (ADR-0016).",
      "properties": {
        "breakeven_at_r": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
              "maximum": 100,
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": 2.0,
          "title": "Breakeven At R"
        },
        "period": {
          "default": 9,
          "maximum": 1000,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Period",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "side": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/SetupSide"
        },
        "stop_buffer_ticks": {
          "default": 0,
          "maximum": 10000,
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Stop Buffer Ticks",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "side"
      ],
      "title": "Mme9BreakoutParams",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Mme9BreakoutSetup": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "params": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Mme9BreakoutParams"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "mme9_breakout",
          "title": "Type",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "params"
      ],
      "title": "Mme9BreakoutSetup",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "NotOf": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Logical NOT. Serialised as `not`, which is a Python keyword — hence the alias.",
      "properties": {
        "not": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Condition"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "not"
      ],
      "title": "NotOf",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Operand": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Ref"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Constant"
        }
      ]
    },
    "PercentRiskParams": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "percent": {
          "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
          "maximum": 100,
          "title": "Percent",
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "percent"
      ],
      "title": "PercentRiskParams",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "PercentRiskSizing": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Size the position so that hitting the stop costs `percent` of the account.",
      "properties": {
        "params": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PercentRiskParams"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "percent_risk",
          "title": "Type",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "params"
      ],
      "title": "PercentRiskSizing",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "PeriodParams": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A window length and nothing else — for the indicators that read the whole candle.\n\n⚠️ Deliberately **not** `PeriodSourceParams` with the source defaulted. ATR is defined over\nhigh, low and the previous close together; a channel is defined over highs and lows. An\n\"ATR of the close\" is not a variant of ATR, it is a different measurement — and a parameter\nthe engine would have to ignore is a request the document believes was honoured.",
      "properties": {
        "period": {
          "maximum": 1000,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Period",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "period"
      ],
      "title": "PeriodParams",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "PeriodSourceParams": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A window length and which price it reads — shared by every single-period indicator\n(SMA, EMA, RSI, and ATR to come). Named for its shape, not for one indicator, because a\nperiod over a price source is exactly what they all take. ATR is *not* one of them — see\n`PeriodParams`.",
      "properties": {
        "period": {
          "maximum": 1000,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Period",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "source": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PriceSource",
          "default": "close"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "period"
      ],
      "title": "PeriodSourceParams",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "PontoContinuoParams": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Two corrections back to the average, then the bar that touches it and closes back.",
      "properties": {
        "average": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/AverageKind",
          "default": "EMA"
        },
        "breakeven_at_r": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
              "maximum": 100,
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": 2.0,
          "title": "Breakeven At R"
        },
        "period": {
          "default": 20,
          "maximum": 1000,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Period",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "side": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/SetupSide"
        },
        "stop_buffer_ticks": {
          "default": 0,
          "maximum": 10000,
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Stop Buffer Ticks",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "side"
      ],
      "title": "PontoContinuoParams",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "PontoContinuoSetup": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "params": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PontoContinuoParams"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "ponto_continuo",
          "title": "Type",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "params"
      ],
      "title": "PontoContinuoSetup",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "PriceSource": {
      "enum": [
        "open",
        "high",
        "low",
        "close"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
    "RSI": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Relative Strength Index — a bounded 0-100 momentum oscillator (Wilder). Same params as a\nmoving average; the engine smooths gains and losses with Wilder's method (ADR-13: adding it\nis additive, so `schema_version` stays 1.0).",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "maxLength": 40,
          "pattern": "^[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*$",
          "title": "Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "params": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PeriodSourceParams"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "RSI",
          "title": "Type",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "type",
        "params"
      ],
      "title": "RSI",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Ref": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A reference to a value the engine can resolve at evaluation time.",
      "properties": {
        "ref": {
          "examples": [
            "sma_fast",
            "price.close",
            "candle[-1].high"
          ],
          "pattern": "^(?:[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*|[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*\\.[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*|price\\.(?:open|high|low|close)|candle\\[-[1-9][0-9]*\\]\\.(?:open|high|low|close))$",
          "title": "Ref",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "ref"
      ],
      "title": "Ref",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Risk": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "max_daily_loss_percent": {
          "default": 3.0,
          "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
          "maximum": 100,
          "title": "Max Daily Loss Percent",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "max_open_positions": {
          "default": 1,
          "maximum": 100,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Max Open Positions",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "sizing": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PercentRiskSizing"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "sizing"
      ],
      "title": "Risk",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "RiskMultipleParams": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "rr": {
          "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
          "maximum": 100,
          "title": "Rr",
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "rr"
      ],
      "title": "RiskMultipleParams",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "RiskMultipleTakeProfit": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Target at N times the distance to the stop.\n\nMeaningless without a stop — there is no risk to take a multiple of. The schema\ncannot say that; `semantic.py` does.",
      "properties": {
        "params": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/RiskMultipleParams"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "risk_multiple",
          "title": "Type",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "params"
      ],
      "title": "RiskMultipleTakeProfit",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "SMA": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "maxLength": 40,
          "pattern": "^[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*$",
          "title": "Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "params": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PeriodSourceParams"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "SMA",
          "title": "Type",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "type",
        "params"
      ],
      "title": "SMA",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Setup": {
      "discriminator": {
        "mapping": {
          "mme9_breakout": "#/$defs/Mme9BreakoutSetup",
          "ponto_continuo": "#/$defs/PontoContinuoSetup",
          "structure_choch": "#/$defs/StructureChochSetup",
          "structure_continuation": "#/$defs/StructureContinuationSetup"
        },
        "propertyName": "type"
      },
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Mme9BreakoutSetup"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PontoContinuoSetup"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/StructureChochSetup"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/StructureContinuationSetup"
        }
      ]
    },
    "SetupSide": {
      "enum": [
        "long",
        "short"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
    "StructureChochSetup": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Trade the zone the change of character left behind.",
      "properties": {
        "params": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/StructureParams"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "structure_choch",
          "title": "Type",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type"
      ],
      "title": "StructureChochSetup",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "StructureContinuationSetup": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Trade the zone a break in the trend's favour leaves behind, after a change of character.",
      "properties": {
        "params": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ContinuationParams"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "structure_continuation",
          "title": "Type",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type"
      ],
      "title": "StructureContinuationSetup",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "StructureParams": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Shared by every setup that arms a limit order on a zone market structure left behind.\n\nNot directional: which side is traded follows the structure, so there is no `side` here.\n`stop_buffer` is a *fraction of the zone's width*, not ticks — the zone is the unit.",
      "properties": {
        "allow_secondary": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Allow Secondary",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "breakeven_at_r": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
              "maximum": 100,
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": 2.0,
          "title": "Breakeven At R"
        },
        "stop_buffer": {
          "default": 0.1,
          "maximum": 10,
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Stop Buffer",
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "title": "StructureParams",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Timeframe": {
      "enum": [
        "M1",
        "M5",
        "M15",
        "M30",
        "H1",
        "H4",
        "D1",
        "W1"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
    "Trend": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Has `of` moved in one direction on each of the last `bars` bars?\n\n⚠️ **Monotonic over the window, not \"higher than it was N bars ago\".** The looser reading\ncalls a series that fell for four bars and jumped on the fifth \"rising\", which is the\nopposite of what anybody writing the rule meant. Matching the reading used by the charting\nplatforms this project's indicators were transcribed from is the point: a rule that means\nsomething different here than on his chart is a rule he cannot check.\n\n`bars: 1` is the base case and the default — \"higher than the previous bar\".",
      "properties": {
        "bars": {
          "default": 1,
          "maximum": 100,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Bars",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "of": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Operand"
        },
        "op": {
          "enum": [
            "rising",
            "falling"
          ],
          "title": "Op",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "op",
        "of"
      ],
      "title": "Trend",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "$id": "https://tradeforge.dev/schema/strategy/v1.json",
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "description": "A complete, self-contained strategy definition.",
  "properties": {
    "description": {
      "default": "",
      "title": "Description",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "entry": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/Entry"
    },
    "exit": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/Exit"
    },
    "indicators": {
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/Indicator"
      },
      "maxItems": 20,
      "title": "Indicators",
      "type": "array"
    },
    "name": {
      "maxLength": 120,
      "minLength": 1,
      "title": "Name",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "risk": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/Risk"
    },
    "schema_version": {
      "const": "1.0",
      "title": "Schema Version",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "setup": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Setup"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null
    },
    "timeframe": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/Timeframe"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "schema_version",
    "name",
    "timeframe",
    "risk"
  ],
  "title": "Strategy",
  "type": "object"
}
